# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Binary Search on Answers is used when the answer lies in a **range**, not in an array.

✅ Look for **monotonic conditions** (once a condition becomes true, it remains true).

✅ Always identify:

- Minimum possible answer
- Maximum possible answer
- Validation function

✅ These problems are among the most frequently asked in product-based company interviews.

---

# 📝 Summary

- Binary Search can be applied to answer spaces.
- Monotonic conditions make Binary Search possible.
- Use a validation function to check whether a candidate answer is feasible.
- Many optimization problems follow this pattern.
- Binary Search on Answers reduces brute-force solutions from **O(N²)** to **O(N log N)** in many cases.

